    </div>

    <h2>What makes Level 39 tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Nine of the sixteen cards end on the mummy. Of the seven that do not, three are where runs stall: step 5 sends the sweet potato from the bag into the mouse hole, step 10 sends the whistle to the girl, and steps 15 and 16 turn the stick into a pillar mechanism. A run that has been treating the mummy as the universal drop target will drag the sweet potato at it, get nothing, and write the bag off as decoration — even though the taser at step 7 comes out of the same bag a moment later.</p>
    <p>That single backpack tap (4) feeds cards five and seven, which is far enough apart to forget. Two more pairs run in lockstep: the match goes to the torch (13) and the torch goes to the mummy (14); the sunflower is double-tapped (8) before the sun can be dragged (9). Neither pair works backwards, and neither is labelled as a pair, so they read as four independent drags on the cards. The torch pair hides a whole move, because lighting it is not the same as using it.</p>
    <p>Most of the inventory is not lying on the floor. A talisman hangs on the wall, the cat is painted on a mural, the cross, the fan and the scarab sit around the room rather than in the bag, and the girl's own shoe is still on her foot (12). A run that scans the ground for loose props finds the backpack and stops looking. The level also finishes away from the mummy — steps 15 and 16 are a slot on the pillar and a downward swipe — so the mummy can look settled while the level is two cards short. The order is the level; the FAQ restates it in a sentence.</p>

    <h2>Three targets and three gates<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Three cards send their item somewhere other than the mummy. Three more have to happen before an item is usable:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The sweet potato (5) goes into the mouse hole, not onto the mummy.</li>
      <li>The whistle (10) goes to the girl.</li>
      <li>The stick (15) goes into the mechanism slot on the pillar, then swipe down (16).</li>
      <li>The backpack tap (4) supplies both the sweet potato (5) and the taser (7).</li>
      <li>Match to torch (13) before torch to mummy (14).</li>
      <li>Double-tap the sunflower (8) before the sun can leave it (9).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Three are about where an item goes and three about what has to happen first, and the three targets all sit late enough in the list to be missed.</p>

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
   
    <details><summary>What is the answer to Brain Puzzle 3 Level 39?</summary><p>In order: 1) Drag the talisman on the wall to the mummy; 2) Drag the cat on the mural to the mummy; 3) Drag the fan to the mummy; 4) Tap the backpack; 5) Drag the sweet potato from the bag to the mouse hole; 6) Drag the cross to the mummy; 7) Drag the taser from the bag to the mummy; 8) Double-tap the sunflower; 9) Drag the sun to the mummy; 10) Drag the whistle to the girl; 11) Drag the scarab to the mummy; 12) Drag the girl's shoe to the mummy; 13) Drag the match to the torch; 14) Drag the torch to the mummy; 15) Drag the stick from the girl's hand to the mechanism slot on the pillar; 16) Swipe down on the stick</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does nothing happen when I tap in Level 39?</summary><p>Three cards in Level 39 are not drags — the tap that opens the backpack at step 4, the double-tap on the sunflower at step 8, and the downward swipe on the stick at step 16 — which is why pressing the mummy does nothing.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is this Level 39 walkthrough up to date?</summary><p>Yes — all sixteen moves follow the current build, from the talisman on the wall to the swipe down on the stick, and older guides can sit a level or two off because inserted levels shift the numbering.</p></details>

